Possco in South Korea acquires Australia’s Sennex Energy, expands overseas gas field business (WoW!Korea) - Yahoo!
Posco International today announced that it has entered into an investment agreement to acquire the shares of Senex Energy in Australia, as well as an investment agreement with Hancock Energy.
The acquisition process is scheduled to be completed in March next year, with procedures such as the approval and approval of a local subsidiary at the General Meeting of Shareholders of Sennex Energy, and the acquisition process is scheduled to be completed in March next year.
Posco International is the world’s largest acquisition and merger (M&A) since it was merged into the Posco Group.
Posco International decided to invest 50.1% and Hancock Energy invests 49.9 percent.
Posco International explained that demand for natural gas will continue to increase even in the era of the energy transition, and in the hydrogen market, natural gas-based blue-hydrogen will divide the market along with green hydrogen.
Posco International will also secure 802 billion cubic cubic cubic 802Bcf natural gas reserves, equivalent to 44% of South Korea's natural gas consumption in 2019, as well as human resources for operations in Australia's land gas field.
