You can actually experience "Kaiji" series of gambling and games (real sound) - Yahoo! News
"Kaiji", a gambling manga series that boasts explosive popularity mainly among men.
One of the real pleasures of this game is that there is a life-threatening game.
[Photo] Just looking at your feet is scooping ... ... Challenge to cross the steel frame!
Therefore, this time I would like to verify the Kaiji's game that can actually be played or practiced in the planning video.
Numa It's a trap-filled pachinko "numa" that appeared in "gambling breaking precepts Kaiji".
According to the original story, Kaiji stunned Kaiji at a high rate of 4000yen per ball.
In this swamp, there were large traps of "nail forest", "movable objects" and "three-stage croon", and it was considered almost impossible to capture.
However, Kaiji used all kinds of hands, and at the end, he put a plastic water tank in the building and went out into the rough business of simmering the ground and tilting it, and captured it brilliantly.
"Numa" that appeared in Kaiji actually appeared as a pachinko, and many people are playing it.
Of course, there is no such thing as "one ball 4000yen", and the difficulty has been lowered, but you will be able to enjoy the feeling of Kaiji.
At a "star side party" held as an entertainment by the rich, it was the steel-frame crossing of "human horse racing" that was carried out by debtors including Kaiji.
The debtor competes for its speed by devising ways not to fall on a thin steel frame set up ten metres above the ground.
There are twelve participants, and the top two can win the prize, but there are only four steelframes, there are not enough safety measures, and the possibility of death is quite high.
In addition to being developed as a VR game, you can have a very close experience at "Eagle Bridge", which is located at "Rakuten Seimei Park Miyagi", the home base of the professional baseball Tohoku Rakuten Golden Eagles.
In this eagle bridge, there is a steel-framed one-of-a-kind bridge at a height of 20m (equivalent to the 7th floor of the building), and "Sky Blanco" and "Victory Ippon Bridge" are prepared at the end, and you are going on your walk.
Of course, safety measures are in place.
Comedian Koala Kogarashi released a video of himself walking on the Eagle Bridge on his YouTube, saying, "You can experience steel-bone crossings in Japan", and it became a hot topic.
"E-Card E-Card", a card game between two people.
A total of ten emperor cards are used, eight citizen's cards, and a total of ten slave cards are used to play, divided into the emperor's side and the slave's side.
This game is very well-crafted and has the characteristics that the emperor is strong against the citizens, the citizens are resistant to the slaves, and the slaves are strong to the emperor.
Kaiji competes against Tonegawa under a strict rule that "if you lose, if you lose, you can shave your own ears."
Kaiji realizes that a device that destroys the ears, such as earphones attached to the ear, is read psychologically by sensing and transmitting changes in the pulse and body temperature, such as an earbud earbud attached after a long struggle.
E-cards are commercially available and can only be purchased on Amazon.
On YouTube, popular YouTuber Hikaru played the role of Kaiji in the movie and uploaded a video in which he competed on an e-card match with Tatsuya Fujiwara, who played the role of Kaiji in the movie, and it attracted a lot of attention.
■Is it possible to taste the Kaiji feeling?
Everyone doesn't want to be in a situation such as Kaiji, but when you read the manga, it is also a fact that you can taste only the mood.
You can feel the world view through the game.
