U.S. tornado "the largest in history" (Nikkan Sports) - Yahoo! News
U.S. tornadoes in the mid-west and in the southern U.S. On Tuesday, U.S. President Joe Biden called it “one of the largest tornadoes in U.S. history.”
This was reported by CNN television.
"We're going to do everything as a federal government," Biden said.
“We still don’t know the full extent of the damage, such as how many lives have been lost,” he said.
More than a hundred people were feared dead.
More than thirty tornadoes have occurred in at least six states, including Kentucky, from the night of the 10th to the dawn of the 11th.
CNN’s meteorological experts estimate that this time it was about two hundred and thirty-seven miles (approximately 350km).
In Mayfield, Kentucky, a candle factory that had been in operation for twenty-four hours in preparation for a Christmas commercial campaign was also severely damaged.
There were 110 people on duty at the time, but the building was destroyed and there was no trace.
In the midst of the darkness, a woman unable to smove under the rubble of about one or five meters thick felt the weight of a rescue worker searching over the rubble and asked for help via a live broadcast on Facebook from her smartphone.
In the live-broadcast, in addition to a woman's cry for help, there was also a "Happy Birthday to You" singing voice, which seems to have been sung while crying in order for another woman's screams to dissipate the fear.
Amber Brown, a convenience store clerk who lives in Mayfield, was safe after she hid in the basement of her five-year-old's home with her five-year-old son due to a tornado warning.
"There are a lot of people comparing it to the sound of a train, but it was a terrible sound like the sound of the ground where something else erupted," he recalled.
A Mayfield police officer said: "We will continue the search operation until it is no longer necessary.
We don’t know if it’s going to be a few weeks, months or years,” he said.
At least six people have been confirmed dead in Illinois as part of a detonated warehouse at home to online shopping giant Amazon.
There have also been a series of lockdowns on highways due to derailment due to the impact of derailing the train's vehicles, as well as due to vehicle falls.
According to U.S. media, about four hundred and forty thousand homes in Tennessee have been without power.
