"Hakobune's seasonal fried fish and prawn fries caught in the near sea Homemade tartar sauce"|Life and Culture|Saga Shimbun News|Saga Shimbun LiVE
Bento "Fry seasonal fish and fried prawns caught in the near sea Homemade tartar sauce"
"hakobune" is a take-out specialty store specializing in colorful bento boxes using plenty of vegetables and deli ( side dishes).
Takayuki Kazuki (39) and Arimi (38) opened the restaurant in August last year.
One of the most popular bento menus is "Frying seasonal fish caught in the near-middle fish and prawn fries Home-made Tartar Sauce" (1000yen).
The fish choose a good one at a time in the market.
"Fry makes raw breadcrumbs as thin as possible so that you can understand the texture of the ingredients," said Takayuki, and you can directly understand the plump texture of fried shrimp.
There are about four kinds of garnished vegetables and a deli in the bento box, as well as rice and soup with millet in the platter rice of Hinohikari produced in Saga Prefecture.
The vegetables are sourced home-made in the buckwheat field or at a direct sales office in the prefecture.
The side dishes change depending on the time of year, but Takayuki has been trained in French cuisine, such as lape and ratatouille to add color.
On the other hand, Arimi-san enjoys "a relaxing taste that you are accustomed to eating" like dashi rolled eggs, and it is a blend of Japanese and Western styles that can be enjoyed by a wide range of generations.
The bent-on lunch box "Kyogo-suki-meat hamburg steak" (1000yen) is also popular.
From next year, we will also release "Charcuterie Set", a processed meat product that goes well with sake such as wine.
