The Importance of Psychiatological Visiting Nurses: Today's Visiting Nursing
Since I suffer from bipolar disorder, I have been receiving home-to-visit nursing care for a long time, but I think that I have a long relationship with the nurse (female) of the visiting nursing station that I am currently using, and I think that I am building a very good relationship.
We talk a lot every week.
Of course, they also do what is necessary for medication management (e.g. packaging, etc.), but more than anything, for those who have a mental illness, I thought about the importance of pleasant communication at today's home-visit nursing.
Today, we also discussed small talk about the gender difference between men and women, or the gender theory.
