South Korea's Samsung Electronics Establishes "DX Division" Integrating Home Appliances and Mobile, Emphasizing the User's Experience (WoW!Korea) - Yahoo! News
Following the integration of the CE and IM divisions as a set division by Samsung Electronics, the company announced on the 12th that the name will be decided as DX (Device eXperience) and that this will be reflected in the organizational reorganization at the end of the year.
The purpose of enhancing the user experience (experience) through a variety of services ranging from mobile devices to home appliances can be seen.
Samsung's DX division, which was newly established by integrating the CE and IM divisions, consists of VD (visual display), household appliances, medical equipment, MX (Mobile eXperience), and the new DX division.
"This name change reflects the medium- to long-term business structure, future orientation, and strengthening of global leadership," a Samsung Electronics official said.
In addition to products such as televisions, home appliances, smartphones, and telecommunications equipment, he emphasized his intention to make it easier for consumers to enjoy an optimized experience through service solutions that reflect the needs of their customers.
With the inauguration of an integrated leadership system, the strategy of creating synergistic synergistic synergistic effects on a company-wide scale and building a platform for differentiated products and services was also reflected in the name.
Samsung Electronics is already working on a strategy that allows users to freely use content and services through inter-equipment-to-equipment, such as home appliances and smartphones based on the Internet of Things (IoT) and artificial intelligence (AI).
