Twenty-four Aichi cars collide Trailer driver has no chronic illness Carelessness (Television Asahi (ANN)) - Yahoo! News
Twenty-four cars collided in Komaki City, Aichi Prefecture, and it was found that the driver of the trailer who had been arrested and was sent off had no chronic illness and seems to have caused an accident due to some inattention.
On the morning of the 10th, twenty-four cars, including a truck and a passenger car, collided on National Route 41 in Komaki City, and twelve people were lightly injured.
The police arrested 54-year-old Katsuya Nomura, who was driving the trailer, on suspicion of injuring a 71-year-old man by causing a rear-end car accident, and sent him to prison on the morning of the 12th.
Mr. Nomura's trailer continued to proceed without stepping on the brakes even after the accident, and the fire department also confirmed that Nomura had temporarily lost consciousness immediately after the accident.
However, according to those involved in the investigation, it was found that Mr. Nomura did not have a chronic illness, and it seems that it was caused by some carelessness.
The police have searched the homes of those involved and are taking a closer look at the situation at the time.
